    portal: show operation queues and review reservations
    
    Expose a bounded read-only Operations view so sessions can identify the
    owner blocking deployment and distinguish resource waits from uncertain
    execution or native notification delivery. Preserve authenticated routes
    and render ledger text through safe DOM operations.

  class Host
    include CodexProviderHost
    include WorkspaceCoordinationHost
    def initialize(env: ENV, input: $stdin, out: $stdout, err: $stderr)
      @env = env
      @input = input
      @out = out
      @err = err
      @home = File.expand_path(env.fetch('HOME'))
      namespace = env.fetch('DEV_WORKSPACES_NAMESPACE', 'dev-workspaces')
      unless namespace.is_a?(String) && namespace.match?(NAME)
        raise Error, "invalid workspace user namespace: #{namespace.inspect}"
      end

      @config = env.fetch('DEV_WORKSPACES_CONFIG', File.join(@home, '.config', namespace, 'registry.json'))
      @state = env.fetch('DEV_WORKSPACES_STATE', File.join(@home, '.local/state', namespace))
      @runtime = env.fetch(
        'DEV_WORKSPACES_RUNTIME_DIR',
        File.join(env.fetch('XDG_RUNTIME_DIR', "/run/user/#{Process.euid}"), namespace)
      )
      @profile = env.fetch('DEV_WORKSPACES_PROFILE', File.join(@state, 'profile'))
      @skills = env.fetch('DEV_WORKSPACES_SKILLS_DIR', File.join(@home, '.codex/skills'))
      @system_codex = codex_for_package(package_root)
      @router_socket = env.fetch(
        'DEV_WORKSPACES_ROUTER_SOCKET',
        '/run/dev-workspaces/router.sock'
      )
    end

    def run(program, argv)
      if program == 'dev-session'
        dispatch(argv, 'dev-session')
        0
      elsif program.end_with?('-devcluster')
      path = transition_lock_file
      FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(path), mode: 0o700)
      raise Error, "workspace transition lock is a symlink: #{path}" if File.symlink?(path)
      File.open(path, File::RDWR | File::CREAT, 0o600) do |file|
        file.flock(mode)
        yield
      end
    end

    def with_current_generation_lock(mode: File::LOCK_EX, allow_first_install: false)
      observed_profile = profile_link_token
      with_transition_lock(mode) do
        uninstalled = !File.exist?(@profile) && !File.symlink?(@profile)
        if observed_profile && profile_link_token != observed_profile
          raise Error,
                'workspace package transition completed while this command waited; rerun it'
        end
        require_current_package_generation! unless allow_first_install && uninstalled
        yield
      end
    end

    # A newer candidate may need to read persisted state that the installed
    # generation cannot parse. Bind its explicit entry to the exact source
    # build, then run the ordinary switch preflight and activation under the
    # same transition lock. No other command can enter from a candidate.
    def with_candidate_generation_lock
      observed_profile = profile_link_token
      with_transition_lock do
        unless observed_profile && profile_link_token == observed_profile &&
               File.symlink?(@profile) &&
               File.executable?(File.join(File.realpath(@profile), 'bin/workspace-host'))
          raise Error, 'selected workspace package changed or is unavailable; rerun the switch'
        end
        yield
      end
    end

    def profile_link_token
      DevWorkspaceProfileIdentity.token(@profile)
    end

    # A failed nix-env invocation can have committed the profile replacement
    # before it reports an error. Read both the profile identity token and its
    # resolved target twice so a retry preserves the only selected authority
    # without accepting a concurrently replaced link.
    def profile_selects_package?(package)
      first_token = profile_link_token
      return false unless first_token && File.symlink?(@profile)

      selected = File.realpath(@profile) == package
      selected && profile_link_token == first_token
    rescue Errno::ENOENT, Errno::EACCES, Errno::ELOOP
      false
    end

    def discard_retired_runtime(retired)
      return unless retired

      FileUtils.remove_entry_secure(retired)
    rescue SystemCallError => e
      @err.puts "warning: unable to remove retired workspace runtime #{retired}: #{e.message}"
    end

    def package_root
      path = File.realpath(__FILE__)
      File.expand_path('..', File.dirname(path))
    end

    def exec_with_workspace(entry, command, *argv, environment: @env.to_h)
      environment = environment.merge('DEV_WORKSPACE_NAME' => entry.fetch('name'))
      exec(environment, command, *argv)
    end
# Coordinated workspace operations

The user-profile coordinator schedules three operations: fast-forward Git
integration, machine activation and workspace profile activation. Sessions keep
their own branches, reviews and conversations. They prepare independently and
submit exact reviewed snapshots under existing user authorization.

Builds, input updates, rebases, conflict resolution and verification run before
resource claims. An admitted worker holds only the resources its mutation needs.
Different repository targets and machines can proceed concurrently. Eligible work
uses FIFO order; waiting on approval or dependencies does not block unrelated work.

## Machine ownership during review

A reservation belongs to a session and physical machine. It survives successful
deployment, idle agents, browser closure, UI review, feedback and repeated fixes.
It also covers workspace profile selection on that machine. Other sessions can
build and merge while their deployment waits.

Normal release requires every exact final owned feature head to be integrated,
all deployed input revisions to be integrated, settled operations and deliveries,
unchanged live identities, and an explicit declaration that deployment and review
work is finished. Integration alone does not release a machine. Deployment or
review does not supply merge approval.

Archive and deletion retain deployed or uncertain reservations as recovery
blockers. Revival preserves ownership. An uncertain effect retains its execution
claim too; a dead process, failed SSH command or timeout cannot prove no effect.
The first implementation refuses exceptional release without integration. Resolve
it through an explicitly authorized, reviewed recovery operation rather than
editing or deleting the ledger.

## Session commands

Commands select the registered workspace normally and require the exact slug:

```text
dev-session coordination status SESSION --as-is --json
dev-session coordination prepare SESSION --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination approve SESSION --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination reserve SESSION --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination submit SESSION --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination refresh SESSION JOB --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination cancel SESSION JOB --as-is --request FILE --json
dev-session coordination reconcile SESSION JOB --as-is --json
This release retains source closures, artifacts, receipts and referenced roots;
it bounds individual logs and admission, not lifetime disk usage. Automatic
source/history pruning is deferred. Never delete an unresolved reservation or
receipt to make room.

A claim without `request.json` predates any worker launch but still requires
operator recovery; this release does not automatically redispatch it. Likewise,
`finish` retains full integration proofs even when deployment was canceled before
activation. Early release without integration is deferred; lifecycle abandonment
or separately reviewed exceptional recovery remains required.

